<!--
  The token endpoint, as a second ProxyEndpoint rather than a flow on the
  first one.

  The reason is the rule the other endpoint is built on. Every control there
  sits in the PreFlow, because a control on a conditional flow is a control
  some requests skip. A token endpoint cannot live under that PreFlow. The
  request that mints a token must not be asked for a token, and the quota is
  keyed on a claim out of the verified token, so on this path the identifier
  resolves to nothing. Putting the mint behind a condition would have been the
  obvious move and it breaks the one invariant that makes the enforcement
  readable off the file.

  So the bundle has two endpoints and each one keeps every control in its own
  PreFlow. The configuration reference says a ProxyEndpoint name "Must be
  unique within the API proxy configuration, when (in rare cases) multiple
  ProxyEndpoints are defined", which is the page acknowledging this shape
  without recommending it.

  The base path does not overlap the other endpoint's. BasePath "must be
  unique within an environment" and the reference says nothing about which
  endpoint serves a request when one base path is a prefix of another. So
  /oauth/v1 rather than /v1/oauth, and the question stays unanswered rather
  than answered by a guess. Same move as the response cache placement.

  There is no TargetEndpoint. "A null RouteRule can be defined to support
  scenarios in which the request message does not need to be forwarded to the
  TargetEndpoint", and the page's own example is <RouteRule name="GoNowhere"/>.
  A mint request reaching the model provider would be a credential handed to a
  backend that has no use for it.
-->
<ProxyEndpoint name="token">
    <PreFlow name="PreFlow">
        <Request>
            <!-- Arrest first, same order and same reason as the other
                 endpoint. An unauthenticated flood against the mint costs a
                 rate check rather than a credential lookup. The identifier is
                 the tenant header, which is caller supplied here and is also
                 caller supplied there. -->
            <Step>
                <Name>SA-PerClient</Name>
            </Step>
            <Step>
                <Name>OA-GenerateToken</Name>
            </Step>
        </Request>
        <Response/>
    </PreFlow>
    <!-- Nothing conditional. A flow here would be a second place to look for
         what is enforced. -->
    <Flows/>
    <PostFlow name="PostFlow">
        <Request/>
        <Response/>
    </PostFlow>
    <HTTPProxyConnection>
        <BasePath>/oauth/v1</BasePath>
    </HTTPProxyConnection>
    <RouteRule name="no-target"/>
</ProxyEndpoint>
